# Source of truth for the curunir container's Python dependencies.
#
# requirements.txt is COMPILED from this file — do not edit it by hand:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt \
#     --generate-hashes --universal --python-version 3.12
#
# `--universal` resolves across platforms with environment markers so one
# lockfile serves both linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 image builds (see
# .github/workflows/build-image.yml). `--generate-hashes` lets the Dockerfile
# install with --require-hashes, so a compromised or substituted artifact on
# PyPI fails the build instead of shipping.
#
# Add CVE floors here (`pkg>=X.Y.Z` with a comment naming the CVE) rather than
# relying on the compile picking up a fix — a bare refresh fixes today and
# silently regresses on the next resolution. Mirrors portal/pyproject.toml.

